            <ArticleTitle>Assessment of bone density in children with Scheuermann's disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>245-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Twenty four children with Scheuermann's disease (11 girls and 13 boys) aged 9-18 years measured for bone mineral density. The total skeleton (TB BMD) and lumbar spine (L2-L4 BMD) mineral density were investigated by dual energy X-ray absorptiometry (DEXA). In nine patients with Scheuermann's disease and backache we found lower levels of TB BMD and L2-L4 BMD in comparison with reference population of Lunar database. Osteopenia in these children may be caused by decreased physical activity due to vertebral pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
